@scene(260, 20)

// One L-shaped profile read twice in the cylindrical coordinate of an axis.
// axisCylindrical gives [distance, u, v] about a line: the distance out from
// it, the angle round it, and the distance along it. On the left the profile
// is revolved: its x is the distance from the axis and its y is v, so the L
// is the section of a flanged sleeve. On the right it is machined on a rotary
// axis: its x is the arc length round the stock, the angle u times the stock's
// radius, and its y is still v, so the L is a pocket wrapped onto a cylinder
// and cut to a depth along the distance. Both axes run along Y.
//
// Each part is coloured by a checkerboard in its own frame, u the angle round
// its axis and v a length: 24 squares round, and checkerSize mm along v. The
// sleeve's frame is revolve's, so its v is the distance along the L's
// outline and the squares follow the section round its corners. The machined
// part's is the rotary axis's, so its v is the distance along the axis and
// the squares run straight across the pocket. Lengths are in mm.

// The L: length and width of its arms, the fillet in the inside corner and
// the round on the heel.
@range(30, 50) armLength = 40.0;
@range(8, 20) armWidth = 14.0;
@range(1, 10) filletRadius = 6.0;
@range(1, 8) heelRadius = 5.0;

// Revolve: distance from the axis to the heel of the L, the sleeve's bore.
@range(2, 30) boreRadius = 10.0;

// Rotary: radius of the stock, and the depth of the pocket.
@range(20, 40) stockRadius = 26.0;
@range(1, 12) pocketDepth = 5.0;

// Checkerboard: the length of a square along v.
@range(2, 12) checkerSize = 6.0;

// Two greys by the parity of the square that (u, v) falls in: 24 squares to
// a turn of u, which is in radians, and checkerSize mm to a square of v.
uvChecker(u, v) {
  return sin(12 * u) * sin(pi * v / checkerSize) > 0 ? color.gray : color.lightGray;
}

// An L with its heel at the origin. A 90 degree corner arc runs between the
// two points one radius back from the sharp corner along each side. The loop
// turns right at the inside corner, so its fillet has negative curvature, and
// left at the heel, so its round has positive.
bracketProfile() {
  return profileXY(
    [[heelRadius, 0], [armLength, 0], [armLength, armWidth],
     [armWidth + filletRadius, armWidth], [armWidth, armWidth + filletRadius],
     [armWidth, armLength], [0, armLength], [0, heelRadius]],
    [0, 0, 0, neg(1 / filletRadius), 0, 0, 0, 1 / heelRadius]);
}

// Revolved about the line x = -boreRadius in the sketch plane, pointing up Y:
// the profile lies on the right of the axis's direction. revolve reads the
// profile at the distance from that line and the distance along it, and gives
// the sleeve its frame: u the angle round the axis, v the profile's own u.
// The sleeve is then moved to put its axis at x = -70.
sleeve = transform.translate(
  revolve(bracketProfile(), [neg(boreRadius), 0], [0, 1]), [boreRadius - 70, 0, 0]);
sleeve.color = uvChecker(sleeve.u, sleeve.v);

// The rotary axis, and the coordinate about it.
rotaryCenter = [60, 0, 0];
rotaryDirection = [0, 1, 0];
rotary = axisCylindrical(rotaryCenter, rotaryDirection);

// The profile's x is the arc length round the stock at its surface, placed so
// the middle of the L faces +Z. Away from the surface an arc is shorter than
// the profile's x by distance / stockRadius, so inside the stock the wrapped
// distance is scaled down to stay a distance.
arcLength = stockRadius * (rotary.y + pi / 2) + armLength / 2;
wrapped = remap(bracketProfile(), [arcLength, rotary.z, 0]) * min(rotary.x / stockRadius, 1);

margin = 8.0;
stock = cylinderCapped(
  rotaryCenter - [0, margin, 0], rotaryCenter + [0, armLength + margin, 0], stockRadius);
pocket = intersectSharp(wrapped, stockRadius - pocketDepth - rotary.x);
machined = differenceSharp(stock, pocket);
machined.u = rotary.y;
machined.v = rotary.z;
machined.color = uvChecker(machined.u, machined.v);

return sleeve, machined;
